/* ═══ AJOUT lot 6 anglais 3e (abonnés) (hors build principal : source à verser dans le dossier des sources) ═══ */
VRT_L("3e-anglais-conditionals",{"titre":"First and second conditionals: real and imaginary situations","duree":35,"famille":"Environment, well-being and health","agir":"Talk about real possibilities and imaginary situations with the first and second conditionals","accroche":"“If it rains, I will stay home.” “If I were the Minister of Environment, I would ban plastic bags.” Same word if, two very different worlds.","intro":"Ngum and her classmates in Bamenda are preparing a debate on climate change. Their sentences will help you understand when to use each conditional.","objectifs":["form the first conditional (if + present, will + verb)","form the second conditional (if + past, would + verb)","choose the right conditional for a real or an imaginary situation","avoid common mistakes (no will after if, were for all persons)"],"enquete":{"titre":"The climate debate in Bamenda","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='Students in a classroom debate: one points to a poster of a flooded street, another holds a placard with a recycling symbol' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='ceC' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#DDEBDA'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F4F1EA'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#ceC)'/><rect y='186' width='640' height='34' fill='#C9A06E'/><rect x='240' y='16' width='170' height='110' fill='#fff' stroke='#9AA3AF'/><rect x='250' y='70' width='150' height='46' fill='#6B8FB0'/><rect x='270' y='40' width='30' height='34' fill='#C46A2B'/><rect x='330' y='46' width='40' height='28' fill='#F2EEE6'/><g transform='translate(130 96)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#2E7D32'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#5A3A1E'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/></g><g transform='translate(500 96)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#1E499B'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#6B4423'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#6B4423'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#6B4423'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#6B4423'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#6B4423'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#6B4423'/></g><rect x='512' y='110' width='40' height='30' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32'/><path d='M524 124l8 -8l8 8' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='3' fill='none'/><rect x='20' y='30' width='200' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#F7C948'/><text x='120' y='50' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>If it rains, …</text><rect x='420' y='20' width='210' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#9FC5E8'/><text x='525' y='40' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>If I were Minister, …</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"In Bamenda, Form 4 students prepare a debate on climate change.","contexte":"<p>Ngum writes: “If it will rain tomorrow, the streets will flood.” Fru writes: “If I am the Minister of Environment, I will ban plastic bags.” Their teacher circles both sentences. Ngum asks: “But what is wrong? Everybody understands!”</p>","documents":[{"t":"Two worlds","html":"<p>Real world: something that can really happen (rain tomorrow). Imaginary world: something that is not true now or is very unlikely (Fru is not the Minister).</p>"}],"question":"When do we use the first conditional and when the second, and how do we form them correctly?","tache":"Learn the form of each conditional, decide if the situation is real or imaginary, then correct Ngum's and Fru's sentences.","hypotheses":["We can use will in both parts of the sentence.","The first and second conditionals mean the same thing.","The first conditional (if + present, will) is for real possibilities; the second (if + past, would) is for imaginary situations; never will after if."]},"parties":[{"t":"The first conditional: real possibilities","html":"<div class='def'><b>First conditional</b>A sentence that talks about a real, possible situation in the present or future and its likely result.</div><p class='formule'>If + present simple, will + base verb</p><ul><li><em>If it rains tomorrow, the streets <strong>will</strong> flood.</em></li><li><em>If we recycle plastic, our town <strong>will</strong> be cleaner.</em></li><li>The <em>if</em>-clause can come second, without a comma: <em>The streets will flood if it rains.</em></li></ul><div class='ex'><b>Example</b><em>If you throw rubbish in the gutter, the water won't flow.</em> (It is a real risk in Bamenda during the rainy season.)</div><div class='attention'><b>French speakers, watch out!</b>Never use <strong>will</strong> in the <em>if</em>-clause: <em>If it <s>will rain</s> rains…</em> French speakers make this mistake because French says « s'il pleut » but thinks in the future.</div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"Building the first conditional","legende":"Two clauses: the condition (if + present) and the result (will + verb). The order can change; with if first, use a comma.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 210' role='img' aria-label='Two columns: condition and result of the first conditional' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>If + present → will + verb</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='299' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='299' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='164.5' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Condition</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>If it rains</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>If we recycle</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>If you study</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ present</text><rect x='326' y='44' width='299' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='326' y='44' width='299' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='475.5' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Result</text><text x='336' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>the streets will flood</text><text x='336' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>the town will be clean</text><text x='336' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>you will pass</text><text x='336' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ will + verb</text><text x='634' y='205' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>Ngum's situation is <strong>real</strong>: it can rain tomorrow. She needs the first conditional, but without <em>will</em> after <em>if</em>: “If it <strong>rains</strong> tomorrow, the streets <strong>will</strong> flood.”</p>","verdicts":[[0,"rejetee","Will never goes in the if-clause: “If it rains”, not “If it will rain”."]]},"retenir":"First conditional: if + present, will + verb (real possibility)."},{"t":"The second conditional: imaginary situations","verrou":true},{"t":"Choosing and using conditionals","verrou":true},{"t":"Vers le BEPC","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","quiz":[],"c":"3e","rang":60,"m":"anglais","payant":true,"apc":{"module":"Environment, Well-Being and Health","famille":"Vie sociale et culturelle","agir":"Communicate about environment, well-being and health","situation":"Ngum writes: “If it will rain tomorrow, the streets will flood.” Fru writes: “If I am the Minister of Environment, I will ban plastic bags.” Their teacher circles both sentences. Ngum asks: “But what is wrong? Everybody understands!”","tache":"Learn the form of each conditional, decide if the situation is real or imaginary, then correct Ngum's and Fru's sentences."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
VRT_L("3e-anglais-reported-speech",{"titre":"Direct and indirect (reported) speech","duree":35,"famille":"Environment, well-being and health","agir":"Report what someone said, changing tenses, pronouns and time words correctly","accroche":"The weather man said: “It will rain tomorrow.” Two days later, you tell your friend: “He said it would rain the next day.” Why did “will” become “would” and “tomorrow” become “the next day”?","intro":"Ekwalla reports the weather forecast he heard on the radio in Limbe. His mistakes will show you the rules of reported speech.","objectifs":["distinguish direct and indirect speech","change tenses when the reporting verb is in the past (backshift)","change pronouns and time and place words","report questions and orders"],"enquete":{"titre":"The weather forecast in Limbe","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='A radio on a table broadcasting the weather; a boy listens, then tells his grandmother on a veranda facing the sea' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='spC' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#BFD9EA'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F4F1EA'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#spC)'/><rect y='150' width='640' height='70' fill='#4A7FA8'/><rect y='186' width='640' height='34' fill='#C9A06E'/><rect x='80' y='120' width='70' height='40' rx='6' fill='#6B4423'/><circle cx='102' cy='140' r='10' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='120' y='130' width='22' height='4' fill='#F7C948'/><g transform='translate(230 100)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#1E499B'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#4A2E1A'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/></g><g transform='translate(420 100)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#5C2D6E'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#5C2D6E'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#7B3F99'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#5A3A1E'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/></g><rect x='40' y='40' width='220' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#F7C948'/><text x='150' y='60' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>“It will rain tomorrow.”</text><rect x='320' y='30' width='280' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#9FC5E8'/><text x='460' y='50' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>He said it would rain the next day.</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"In Limbe, Ekwalla tells his grandmother what the radio said.","contexte":"<p>The radio said: “It will rain heavily tomorrow. Fishermen must stay on shore.” The next day, Ekwalla tells his grandmother: “The radio said it will rain heavily tomorrow and that fishermen must stay on shore.” His English teacher, who heard him, says: “Your message is right, but your grammar is not reported speech yet.”</p>","documents":[{"t":"Two ways of reporting","html":"<p>Direct speech repeats the exact words between quotation marks. Indirect (reported) speech gives the meaning, without quotation marks, and adapts tenses, pronouns and time words.</p>"}],"question":"How do we change direct speech into indirect speech correctly?","tache":"Learn the backshift of tenses, the changes of pronouns and time words, then correct Ekwalla's report.","hypotheses":["In reported speech, we just remove the quotation marks.","We change only the pronouns, never the tenses.","When the reporting verb is in the past, tenses go one step back, and pronouns and time words change to fit the new situation."]},"parties":[{"t":"Direct and indirect speech","html":"<div class='def'><b>Direct speech</b>The exact words of a speaker, between quotation marks: <em>He said, “I am tired.”</em></div><div class='def'><b>Indirect (reported) speech</b>The words of a speaker reported without quotation marks, usually after <em>say</em> or <em>tell</em>, often with <em>that</em>: <em>He said (that) he was tired.</em></div><ul><li><strong>say</strong> + (that) : <em>She said that she was hungry.</em></li><li><strong>tell</strong> + person + (that) : <em>She told me that she was hungry.</em></li></ul><p class='formule'>reporting verb (said / told me) + that + reported clause</p><div class='ex'><b>Example</b>Direct: <em>Ngum said, “I like football.”</em> → Indirect: <em>Ngum said (that) she liked football.</em></div><div class='attention'><b>French speakers, watch out!</b><em>Say</em> has no person object: not « he said me » but <em>he told me</em> or <em>he said to me</em>.</div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"From direct to indirect","legende":"Quotation marks disappear; a reporting verb and that introduce the reported clause.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 200' role='img' aria-label='Two columns: direct and indirect speech' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='200' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='200' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Two ways of reporting</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='299' height='142' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='299' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='164.5' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Direct</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>exact words</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>“quotation marks”</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>He said, “I am…”</text><rect x='326' y='44' width='299' height='142' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='326' y='44' width='299' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='475.5' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Indirect</text><text x='336' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>meaning</text><text x='336' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>no quotation marks</text><text x='336' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>He said that he was…</text><text x='634' y='195' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>Ekwalla removed the quotation marks, but he kept “will” and “tomorrow”. That is not enough: reported speech also changes <strong>tenses</strong> and <strong>time words</strong>.</p>","verdicts":[[0,"rejetee","Removing the quotation marks is not enough: tenses and time words change too."]]},"retenir":"Direct: exact words in quotes; indirect: say / tell + that, adapted words."},{"t":"Backshift: changing the tenses","verrou":true},{"t":"Pronouns, time words, questions and orders","verrou":true,"illus":{"legende":"Time words in reported speech. When we report later, words that point to the moment of speaking must change.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 230' role='img' aria-label='Three columns: time words, place words and questions in reported speech' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='230' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='230' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Direct → reported</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='172' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='112.66666666666667' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Time</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>today → that day</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>tomorrow → the next day</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>yesterday → the day before</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>now → then</text><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='172' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='320' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Place</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>here → there</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>this → that</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>these → those</text><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='172' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C2540A'/><text x='527.3333333333334' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Questions</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>“Are you…?” →</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>asked if I was</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>“Where…?” →</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>asked where I lived</text><text x='634' y='225' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}},{"t":"Vers le BEPC","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","quiz":[],"c":"3e","rang":57,"m":"anglais","payant":true,"apc":{"module":"Environment, Well-Being and Health","famille":"Vie sociale et culturelle","agir":"Communicate about environment, well-being and health","situation":"The radio said: “It will rain heavily tomorrow. Fishermen must stay on shore.” The next day, Ekwalla tells his grandmother: “The radio said it will rain heavily tomorrow and that fishermen must stay on shore.” His English teacher, who heard him, says: “Your message is right, but your grammar is not reported speech yet.”","tache":"Learn the backshift of tenses, the changes of pronouns and time words, then correct Ekwalla's report."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
VRT_L("3e-anglais-passive-voice",{"titre":"Active and passive voices","duree":35,"famille":"Citizenship and human rights","agir":"Change sentences from the active to the passive voice and choose the voice that fits the message","accroche":"“Workers in Douala make chocolate.” “Chocolate is made in Douala.” Same fact, two voices. Why would a journalist choose the second?","intro":"Mbah writes an article for the school magazine about a cocoa factory in Douala. His sentences will help you master the passive voice.","objectifs":["recognise the active and the passive voice","form the passive (be + past participle) in the main tenses","use by + agent only when necessary","choose the voice according to what is important in the message"],"enquete":{"titre":"The school magazine article","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='A factory hall with a conveyor belt carrying bags of cocoa beans that come out as chocolate bars; a student journalist takes notes' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='paC2' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#E3EAF4'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F4F1EA'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#paC2)'/><rect y='186' width='640' height='34' fill='#8F8A80'/><rect x='120' y='130' width='400' height='14' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='150' y='108' width='40' height='22' fill='#8B5A2B'/><rect x='230' y='108' width='40' height='22' fill='#8B5A2B'/><rect x='360' y='108' width='40' height='22' fill='#4A2511'/><rect x='450' y='108' width='40' height='22' fill='#4A2511'/><rect x='290' y='70' width='50' height='60' fill='#C9CED6'/><g transform='translate(70 100)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#1E499B'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#1E499B'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#F4F1EA'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#F4F1EA' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#F4F1EA' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#5A3A1E'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/></g><rect x='86' y='126' width='20' height='26' fill='#fff' stroke='#9AA3AF'/><rect x='20' y='20' width='260' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#F7C948'/><text x='150' y='40' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Chocolate is made here…</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"In Douala, Mbah visits a cocoa processing factory for the school magazine.","contexte":"<p>Mbah writes: “Somebody grows the cocoa in the South Region. Somebody makes the chocolate here. People have exported the chocolate to Nigeria by people.” His teacher comments: “Too many ‘somebody’! Use the passive voice, and don't write ‘by people’.”</p>","documents":[{"t":"Two voices","html":"<p>In the active voice, the subject does the action. In the passive voice, the subject receives the action; the doer (agent) is introduced by <em>by</em> or left out.</p>"}],"question":"How do we form the passive voice, and when should we use it?","tache":"Form the passive in the main tenses, decide when to keep or remove the agent, then rewrite Mbah's article.","hypotheses":["The passive is just the active with by added at the end.","We must always mention the agent with by.","The passive is be (in the tense of the active verb) + past participle; we use it when the action matters more than the doer, and we drop the agent when it is unknown or obvious."]},"parties":[{"t":"Active and passive voices","html":"<div class='def'><b>Active voice</b>The subject does the action: <em><u>Workers</u> make chocolate.</em></div><div class='def'><b>Passive voice</b>The subject receives the action: <em><u>Chocolate</u> is made (by workers).</em> The object of the active sentence becomes the subject of the passive sentence.</div><p class='formule'>passive = be (same tense as the active verb) + past participle (+ by + agent)</p><div class='ex'><b>Example</b>Active: <em>Farmers grow cocoa in the South Region.</em> → Passive: <em>Cocoa is grown in the South Region (by farmers).</em></div><div class='attention'><b>Watch out!</b>Only verbs with an object can become passive: « The bus arrived » has no passive.</div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"From active to passive","legende":"The object moves to the front, the verb becomes be + past participle, and the subject becomes the agent (by…), often dropped.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 210' role='img' aria-label='Two columns: active and passive sentence' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Active → passive</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='299' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='299' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='164.5' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Active</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Workers</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>make</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>chocolate.</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ subject acts</text><rect x='326' y='44' width='299' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='326' y='44' width='299' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='475.5' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Passive</text><text x='336' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Chocolate</text><text x='336' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>is made</text><text x='336' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>(by workers).</text><text x='336' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ subject receives</text><text x='634' y='205' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>“Somebody grows the cocoa” tells us nothing about the doer: the important thing is the cocoa. The passive puts it first: “The cocoa <strong>is grown</strong> in the South Region.”</p>","verdicts":[[0,"rejetee","The passive is not just “by” added: the object becomes the subject and the verb becomes be + past participle."]]},"retenir":"Passive: object → subject; be + past participle; by + agent."},{"t":"The passive in the main tenses","verrou":true},{"t":"When to use the passive and the agent","verrou":true},{"t":"Vers le BEPC","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","quiz":[],"c":"3e","rang":80,"m":"anglais","payant":true,"apc":{"module":"Citizenship/Human Rights","famille":"Vie sociale et culturelle","agir":"Communicate about citizenship/human rights","situation":"Mbah writes: “Somebody grows the cocoa in the South Region. Somebody makes the chocolate here. People have exported the chocolate to Nigeria by people.” His teacher comments: “Too many ‘somebody’! Use the passive voice, and don't write ‘by people’.”","tache":"Form the passive in the main tenses, decide when to keep or remove the agent, then rewrite Mbah's article."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
VRT_L("3e-anglais-relative-clauses",{"titre":"Relative clauses: who, which, that, whose, where","duree":35,"famille":"Environment, well-being and health","agir":"Join two sentences with a relative pronoun to describe people, things and places","accroche":"“I met a girl. The girl plants trees.” → “I met a girl who plants trees.” One small word joins two sentences. Which word, and when?","intro":"Siri writes a report on an environmental club in Garoua. Her short, repeated sentences will help you learn relative clauses.","objectifs":["identify a relative clause","choose the right relative pronoun (who, which, that, whose, where)","join two sentences with a relative pronoun","punctuate defining and non-defining relative clauses"],"enquete":{"titre":"Siri's report on the green club","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='Students planting trees beside a school; a girl writes in a notebook; a bridge over a small river joins two banks' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='rlC' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#DDEBDA'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F4F1EA'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#rlC)'/><rect y='160' width='640' height='60' fill='#4A90C0'/><rect x='0' y='150' width='240' height='70' fill='#7FA347'/><rect x='400' y='150' width='240' height='70' fill='#B9B3A6'/><rect x='240' y='146' width='160' height='8' fill='#C9A04A'/><rect x='57' y='110' width='6' height='40' fill='#5C3A1E'/><circle cx='60' cy='104' r='16' fill='#2E7D32'/><rect x='117' y='110' width='6' height='40' fill='#5C3A1E'/><circle cx='120' cy='104' r='16' fill='#2E7D32'/><rect x='177' y='110' width='6' height='40' fill='#5C3A1E'/><circle cx='180' cy='104' r='16' fill='#2E7D32'/><rect x='450' y='100' width='120' height='50' fill='#F2EEE6'/><path d='M440 104L510 76L580 104Z' fill='#C46A2B'/><g transform='translate(300 60)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#5C2D6E'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#5C2D6E'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#7B3F99'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#6B4423'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#6B4423'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#6B4423'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#6B4423'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#6B4423'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#6B4423'/></g><rect x='330' y='16' width='280' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#F7C948'/><text x='470' y='36' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>…a club who / which / that…?</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"In Garoua, Siri writes about her school's environmental club.","contexte":"<p>Siri writes: “Our school has a club. The club plants trees. The club's president is Aminatou. Aminatou loves nature. We plant trees near the river. The river is polluted.” Her teacher says: “Join these sentences with relative pronouns.” Siri writes: “Our school has a club who plants trees.” The teacher circles “who”.</p>","documents":[{"t":"Relative pronouns","html":"<p>A relative pronoun (who, which, that, whose, where) joins two sentences and introduces a relative clause that gives information about a noun.</p>"}],"question":"How do we join sentences with relative pronouns, and which pronoun goes with people, things and places?","tache":"Learn each relative pronoun, join Siri's sentences, then punctuate the relative clauses correctly.","hypotheses":["Who can be used for everything: people, things and animals.","Relative pronouns are useless: short sentences are clearer.","Who is for people, which for things and animals, that for both, whose for possession, where for places; relative clauses join ideas and avoid repetition."]},"parties":[{"t":"What is a relative clause?","html":"<div class='def'><b>Relative clause</b>A part of a sentence introduced by a relative pronoun (who, which, that, whose, where) that gives information about a noun just before it (the antecedent).</div><p class='formule'>noun (antecedent) + relative pronoun + rest of the clause</p><ul><li><em>I met a girl. The girl plants trees.</em> → <em>I met a girl <strong>who</strong> plants trees.</em></li><li>The relative pronoun replaces the repeated noun: we do not repeat it (« a girl who <s>she</s> plants trees »).</li></ul><div class='ex'><b>Example</b><em>The tree <strong>that</strong> we planted is growing.</em> — antecedent: <em>the tree</em>; relative clause: <em>that we planted</em>.</div><div class='attention'><b>French speakers, watch out!</b>Do not add a second pronoun: not « the man who he came », but <em>the man who came</em>.</div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"Joining two sentences","legende":"The repeated noun disappears and the relative pronoun takes its place, just after the noun it describes.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 200' role='img' aria-label='Three columns: two sentences joined by a relative pronoun' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='200' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='200' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Two sentences → one</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='142' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='112.66666666666667' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Sentence 1</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Our school has</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>a club.</text><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='142' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C2540A'/><text x='320' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Sentence 2</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>The club</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>plants trees.</text><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='142' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='527.3333333333334' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Joined</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Our school has a club</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>which / that</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>plants trees.</text><text x='634' y='195' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>Siri's idea is good: one sentence instead of two. But the club is <strong>not a person</strong>: “who” is wrong here.</p>","verdicts":[[1,"rejetee","Relative clauses join ideas and avoid repetition: they make writing better, not worse."]]},"retenir":"Relative clause: antecedent + relative pronoun + clause; do not repeat the noun."},{"t":"Choosing the relative pronoun","verrou":true},{"t":"Defining and non-defining clauses","verrou":true},{"t":"Vers le BEPC","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","quiz":[],"c":"3e","rang":54,"m":"anglais","payant":true,"apc":{"module":"Environment, Well-Being and Health","famille":"Vie sociale et culturelle","agir":"Communicate about environment, well-being and health","situation":"Siri writes: “Our school has a club. The club plants trees. The club's president is Aminatou. Aminatou loves nature. We plant trees near the river. The river is polluted.” Her teacher says: “Join these sentences with relative pronouns.” Siri writes: “Our school has a club who plants trees.” The teacher circles “who”.","tache":"Learn each relative pronoun, join Siri's sentences, then punctuate the relative clauses correctly."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
