VRT_L("3e-anglais-comparatives",{"titre":"Comparatives and superlatives: choosing a restaurant","famille":"Economic life and occupations","agir":"Compare places, prices and services to make a good choice","accroche":"“Mami Ekwe's restaurant is more cheaper than the Seaview!” Eposi's idea is clear… but her sentence is wrong: one word too many.","intro":"In Limbe, Eposi and Tabi must choose a restaurant for their class party. Their comparisons will show you how to compare correctly in English.","objectifs":["form the comparative of short adjectives (cheap → cheaper than)","form the comparative of long adjectives (expensive → more expensive than)","use the irregular forms good, bad and far","form the superlative and compare with as … as"],"enquete":{"titre":"The class party in Limbe","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='Two students in front of two restaurants by the sea: a small one with a price board and a big one with a terrace' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='cpC' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#DCEBF5'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F6F1E7'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#cpC)'/><rect y='186' width='640' height='34' fill='#D8C49A'/><rect x='0' y='150' width='640' height='36' fill='#6FA8C9'/><rect x='200' y='70' width='110' height='90' fill='#F2E3C6' stroke='#9A7B4F'/><rect x='200' y='60' width='110' height='16' fill='#C46A2B'/><text x='255' y='72' text-anchor='middle' font-size='9' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>MAMI EKWE</text><rect x='215' y='92' width='36' height='26' fill='#fff' stroke='#9A7B4F'/><text x='233' y='109' text-anchor='middle' font-size='9' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>1 500</text><rect x='330' y='50' width='150' height='110' fill='#fff' stroke='#7C8DB5'/><rect x='330' y='40' width='150' height='16' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='405' y='52' text-anchor='middle' font-size='9' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>SEAVIEW GRILL</text><rect x='345' y='80' width='40' height='30' fill='#BFD7EA'/><rect x='425' y='80' width='40' height='30' fill='#BFD7EA'/><text x='405' y='140' text-anchor='middle' font-size='9' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>3 500</text><g transform='translate(130 96)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#5C2D6E'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#5C2D6E'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#7B3F99'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#5A3A1E'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/></g><g transform='translate(510 96)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#17784D'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#17784D' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#17784D' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#6B4423'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#6B4423'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#6B4423'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#6B4423'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#6B4423'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#6B4423'/></g><rect x='20' y='26' width='230' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#F7C948'/><text x='135' y='46' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Mami Ekwe's is more cheaper!</text><rect x='400' y='26' width='230' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#9FC5E8'/><text x='515' y='46' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>And the most good, maybe?</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"In Limbe, Eposi and Tabi compare two restaurants for their end-of-term party.","contexte":"<p>Eposi writes a note for the class WhatsApp group: “Mami Ekwe's restaurant is more cheaper than the Seaview Grill. It is also the most good place in Limbe, and the food is more hot. The Seaview is more far from school.” Tabi answers: “Your ideas are good, but your English is not! Our teacher will laugh.”</p>","documents":[{"t":"Tabi's notes on the two restaurants","html":"<p><strong>Mami Ekwe's</strong>: ndolé and plantain, 1 500 FCFA a plate; 10 minutes' walk from school; 40 seats; food very spicy; students' rating 4/5.<br><strong>Seaview Grill</strong>: grilled fish, 3 500 FCFA a plate; 25 minutes by taxi; 120 seats; beautiful view of the sea; students' rating 3/5.</p>"}],"question":"How do we compare two or more places correctly in English?","tache":"Learn the rules of comparatives and superlatives, then rewrite Eposi's note without mistakes.","hypotheses":["We can put more before every adjective, even when it already ends in -er.","Comparatives and superlatives are the same thing: we can use one for the other.","Short adjectives take -er / the -est, long adjectives take more / the most, and good, bad and far are irregular."]},"parties":[{"t":"Comparatives of short adjectives","html":"<div class='def'><b>Comparative</b>The form of an adjective used to compare <strong>two</strong> people, places or things: <em>cheaper than</em>, <em>more expensive than</em>.</div><p class='formule'>short adjective + -er + than</p><ul><li>One syllable: add <strong>-er</strong>: <em>cheap → cheaper</em>, <em>small → smaller</em>, <em>fast → faster</em>.</li><li>Ending in <strong>-e</strong>: add <strong>-r</strong>: <em>large → larger</em>, <em>nice → nicer</em>, <em>safe → safer</em>.</li><li>One short vowel + one consonant: <strong>double</strong> the consonant: <em>big → bigger</em>, <em>hot → hotter</em>, <em>thin → thinner</em>.</li><li>Two syllables ending in <strong>-y</strong>: y becomes <strong>i</strong>: <em>busy → busier</em>, <em>tasty → tastier</em>, <em>easy → easier</em>.</li></ul><div class='ex'><b>Example</b>Mami Ekwe's ndolé (1 500 FCFA) is <strong>cheaper than</strong> the Seaview's grilled fish (3 500 FCFA). Mami Ekwe's food is <strong>hotter</strong> (spicier) too.</div><div class='attention'><b>French speakers, watch out!</b>French always says « plus cher ». English uses <strong>-er</strong> OR <strong>more</strong>, never both: <s>more cheaper</s> → <strong>cheaper</strong>.</div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"Short adjectives: four spelling rules","legende":"Read each column from top to bottom: the last line gives the rule. Most mistakes come from the double consonant and the -y ending.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 200' role='img' aria-label='Four columns of short adjectives and their comparatives' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='200' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='200' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Short adjective + -er + than</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='143.5' height='142' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='143.5' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='86.75' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Add -er</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>cheap → cheaper</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>small → smaller</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>fast → faster</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ + er</text><rect x='170.5' y='44' width='143.5' height='142' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#17784D' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='170.5' y='44' width='143.5' height='34' rx='11' fill='#17784D'/><text x='242.25' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Ends in -e</text><text x='180.5' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>large → larger</text><text x='180.5' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>nice → nicer</text><text x='180.5' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>safe → safer</text><text x='180.5' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#17784D'>→ + r</text><rect x='326' y='44' width='143.5' height='142' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='326' y='44' width='143.5' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C2540A'/><text x='397.75' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Double</text><text x='336' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>big → bigger</text><text x='336' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>hot → hotter</text><text x='336' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>thin → thinner</text><text x='336' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C2540A'>→ double + er</text><rect x='481.5' y='44' width='143.5' height='142' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='481.5' y='44' width='143.5' height='34' rx='11' fill='#7B3F99'/><text x='553.25' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Ends in -y</text><text x='491.5' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>busy → busier</text><text x='491.5' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>tasty → tastier</text><text x='491.5' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>easy → easier</text><text x='491.5' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#7B3F99'>→ y → ier</text><text x='634' y='195' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>First clue: <em>cheap</em> has one syllable, so it takes -er alone: “Mami Ekwe's is <strong>cheaper than</strong> the Seaview.” “More cheaper” puts two comparatives together. In the same way, <em>more hot</em> becomes <strong>hotter</strong>.</p>","verdicts":[[0,"rejetee","More never goes with -er: cheaper, not more cheaper; hotter, not more hot."]]},"retenir":"Short adjectives: adjective + -er + than (cheaper than, bigger than, tastier than)."},{"t":"Long adjectives and irregular forms","verrou":true},{"t":"Superlatives and comparisons of equality","verrou":true},{"t":"Vers le BEPC","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","c":"3e","m":"anglais","rang":28,"payant":true,"duree":35,"quiz":[],"apc":{"module":"Economic Life and Occupations","famille":"Vie économique","agir":"Communicate about economic life and occupations","situation":"Eposi, a Form 4 student in Limbe, writes to her class group: “Mami Ekwe's restaurant is more cheaper than the Seaview Grill. It is also the most good place in Limbe, and the food is more hot. The Seaview is more far from school.” The class must choose a restaurant for the end-of-term party.","tache":"Correct Eposi's note, then compare the two restaurants with at least two comparatives and one superlative."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
VRT_L("3e-anglais-complex-sentences",{"titre":"Complex sentences: coordination and subordination for best buys","famille":"Economic life and occupations","agir":"Link ideas clearly to explain good choices when buying","accroche":"“Although the phone is cheap, but I did not buy it.” In French, « bien que… mais » sounds wrong too. In English, one linking word is enough.","intro":"At Mokolo market in Yaoundé, Ayissi compares two phones before buying one. His advice to his classmates will teach you how to join ideas in one sentence.","objectifs":["recognise simple, compound and complex sentences","join two main clauses with a coordinator (and, but, or, so)","add a subordinate clause with a subordinator (because, although, when, if, so that)","avoid two linking words for one link (although … but) and because of + clause"],"enquete":{"titre":"Ayissi's shopping advice","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='Two students at a market stall full of phones and price labels' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='csC' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#F3E7D3'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F8F4EC'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#csC)'/><rect y='186' width='640' height='34' fill='#B98E5E'/><rect x='220' y='96' width='200' height='60' fill='#8A5A2B'/><rect x='210' y='60' width='220' height='14' fill='#C62828'/><rect x='214' y='74' width='4' height='82' fill='#5C3D22'/><rect x='422' y='74' width='4' height='82' fill='#5C3D22'/><rect x='240' y='104' width='26' height='40' rx='4' fill='#1F2328'/><rect x='244' y='108' width='18' height='30' fill='#6B8FB0'/><rect x='300' y='104' width='26' height='40' rx='4' fill='#1F2328'/><rect x='304' y='108' width='18' height='30' fill='#9FC5E8'/><rect x='360' y='104' width='44' height='22' fill='#fff' stroke='#9A7B4F'/><text x='382' y='119' text-anchor='middle' font-size='9' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>1 YEAR</text><text x='253' y='165' text-anchor='middle' font-size='9' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>35 000</text><text x='313' y='165' text-anchor='middle' font-size='9' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>48 000</text><g transform='translate(130 96)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#1E499B'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2F1A'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2F1A'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#4A2F1A'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#4A2F1A'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2F1A'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2F1A'/></g><g transform='translate(510 96)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#7A3A10'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#7A3A10'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#C2540A'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#6B4423'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#6B4423'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#6B4423'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#6B4423'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#6B4423'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#6B4423'/></g><rect x='20' y='26' width='230' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#F7C948'/><text x='135' y='46' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Although it's cheap, but…</text><rect x='400' y='26' width='230' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#9FC5E8'/><text x='515' y='46' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>One link word is enough!</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"At Mokolo market, Ayissi compares two phones: one cheap without a guarantee, one dearer with a one-year guarantee.","contexte":"<p>Ayissi writes advice for the class magazine: “The first phone is cheap. It has no guarantee. Although it is cheap, but I did not buy it. I bought the other one. It was more expensive. I bought it because of it has a one-year guarantee.” His English teacher writes in the margin: “Good ideas, but your sentences are like a telegram, and two of them are wrong. Join your ideas correctly.”</p>","documents":[{"t":"The two phones at the stall","html":"<p>Phone A: 35 000 FCFA, no guarantee, no receipt. Phone B: 48 000 FCFA, one-year guarantee, receipt given, free repair during the first year.</p>"}],"question":"How can we join two ideas in one correct sentence?","tache":"Learn the two ways of joining clauses, then rewrite Ayissi's advice in four correct sentences.","hypotheses":["Short sentences are always better: we should never join them.","We can use although and but together, like « bien que… mais ».","Coordinators (and, but, or, so) join two equal clauses; subordinators (because, although, when, if) add a dependent clause; one link needs only one linking word."]},"parties":[{"t":"Simple, compound and complex sentences","html":"<div class='def'><b>Complex sentence</b>A sentence made of a <strong>main clause</strong> and at least one <strong>subordinate clause</strong> introduced by a subordinator: <em>I bought this phone <u>because it has a guarantee</u>.</em></div><ul><li>A <strong>clause</strong> is a group of words with a subject and a conjugated verb: <em>the phone is cheap</em>.</li><li>A <strong>simple sentence</strong> has one clause: <em>The phone is cheap.</em></li><li>A <strong>compound sentence</strong> joins two main clauses with a coordinator: this is <strong>coordination</strong>: <em>The phone is cheap, but it has no guarantee.</em></li><li>A <strong>complex sentence</strong> adds a subordinate clause to a main clause: this is <strong>subordination</strong>: <em>I did not buy it because it had no guarantee.</em></li></ul><p class='formule'>simple = 1 clause · compound = main + coordinator + main · complex = main + subordinator + subordinate</p><div class='attention'><b>Watch out!</b>A subordinate clause alone is not a sentence: <s>Because it has a guarantee.</s> It needs a main clause: <em>I chose it because it has a guarantee.</em></div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"Three kinds of sentences","legende":"The kind of sentence depends on the number of clauses and on the word that joins them.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 180' role='img' aria-label='Three columns: simple, compound and complex sentences' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='180' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='180' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>One clause, two equal clauses, or main + subordinate?</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='122' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#7C8DB5' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#7C8DB5'/><text x='112.66666666666667' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Simple</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>The phone is cheap.</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>It has no guarantee.</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#7C8DB5'>→ one clause</text><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='122' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='320' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Compound</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>The phone is cheap,</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>but it has no guarantee.</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ coordination</text><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='122' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#17784D' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#17784D'/><text x='527.3333333333334' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Complex</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>I chose phone B</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>because it has a guarantee.</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#17784D'>→ subordination</text><text x='634' y='175' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>First clue: Ayissi's short sentences are correct, but they do not show the <strong>links</strong> between his ideas: contrast (cheap / no guarantee), reason (he chose phone B because of the guarantee). Joining clauses makes the logic visible.</p>","verdicts":[[0,"rejetee","Short sentences are correct, but joining them shows how the ideas are related."]]},"retenir":"Clause = subject + verb; compound sentence = coordination; complex sentence = subordination."},{"t":"Coordination: and, but, or, so","verrou":true},{"t":"Subordination: because, although, when, if, so that","verrou":true},{"t":"Vers le BEPC","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","c":"3e","m":"anglais","rang":34,"payant":true,"duree":35,"quiz":[],"apc":{"module":"Economic Life and Occupations","famille":"Vie économique","agir":"Communicate about economic life and occupations","situation":"At Mokolo market, Ayissi compared two phones: phone A at 35 000 FCFA without a guarantee, phone B at 48 000 FCFA with a one-year guarantee. His advice for the class magazine reads: “The first phone is cheap. It has no guarantee. Although it is cheap, but I did not buy it. I bought it because of it has a one-year guarantee.”","tache":"Rewrite Ayissi's advice in correct sentences, using at least one coordinator and two subordinators."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
VRT_L("3e-anglais-gerunds",{"titre":"Gerunds: talking about leisure activities","famille":"Economic life and occupations","agir":"Talk about one's leisure activities, likes and dislikes","accroche":"“I enjoy to play football.” Every student understands it, yet no English speaker says it. After enjoy, the verb takes -ing.","intro":"In Garoua, Hamadou fills in a profile to find a pen friend in Buea. His sentences will show you when English uses a verb in -ing as a noun: the gerund.","objectifs":["recognise a gerund and spell the -ing form correctly","use a gerund as the subject of a sentence","use the gerund after verbs like enjoy, finish, avoid, mind","use the gerund after prepositions (interested in, good at, look forward to)"],"enquete":{"titre":"Hamadou's pen-friend profile","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='A student fills in a profile on a computer while a friend points to a football and a sketchbook' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='geC' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#FBEBD0'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F8F4EC'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#geC)'/><rect y='186' width='640' height='34' fill='#D9B98A'/><rect x='250' y='70' width='140' height='90' rx='6' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='258' y='78' width='124' height='70' fill='#E6EEF8'/><text x='320' y='96' text-anchor='middle' font-size='10' font-weight='700' fill='#1E499B'>MY PROFILE</text><rect x='268' y='104' width='104' height='6' fill='#C9D2E3'/><rect x='268' y='116' width='80' height='6' fill='#C9D2E3'/><rect x='268' y='128' width='92' height='6' fill='#C9D2E3'/><rect x='300' y='160' width='40' height='8' fill='#2E3445'/><circle cx='430' cy='170' r='14' fill='#fff' stroke='#1F2328'/><path d='M424 164l6 4l6 -4l-2 8h-8z' fill='#1F2328'/><rect x='180' y='150' width='40' height='30' fill='#fff' stroke='#7B3F99'/><path d='M186 172l8 -12l8 8l8 -6' stroke='#7B3F99' fill='none' stroke-width='2'/><g transform='translate(130 96)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#17784D'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#17784D' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#17784D' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#3F2A18'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#3F2A18'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#3F2A18'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#3F2A18'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#3F2A18'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#3F2A18'/></g><g transform='translate(510 96)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#6B4E1E'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#6B4E1E'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#C9A04A'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#C9A04A' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#C9A04A' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#5A3A1E'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/></g><rect x='20' y='26' width='230' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#F7C948'/><text x='135' y='46' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>I enjoy to play football.</text><rect x='400' y='26' width='230' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#9FC5E8'/><text x='515' y='46' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Enjoy + -ing, Hamadou!</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"In Garoua, Hamadou describes his leisure activities to find a pen friend.","contexte":"<p>Hamadou's profile says: “Hello! My name is Hamadou. I am 15 and I live in Garoua. I enjoy to play football with my friends near the Benue. I am interested in draw. Swim is my favourite activity in the holidays. I want visiting Buea one day. I look forward to meet you!” His cousin Aïssatou reads it and says: “Your activities are nice, but five verbs are in the wrong form.”</p>","documents":[{"t":"Aïssatou's list of Hamadou's leisure activities","html":"<p>football (with friends, every Saturday) · drawing (comics) · swimming (in the holidays) · dancing at family ceremonies · watching cartoons</p>"}],"question":"When must a verb take the -ing form in English, and when does it take to?","tache":"Learn when English uses the gerund, then correct the five mistakes in Hamadou's profile.","hypotheses":["After every verb, we use to + verb: enjoy to play, want to visit.","A verb can never be the subject of a sentence: “Swim is my favourite activity” is correct.","As a subject, after some verbs (enjoy, finish, avoid…) and after prepositions, English uses the gerund (verb + -ing); other verbs (want, decide, hope) take to."]},"parties":[{"t":"What is a gerund?","html":"<div class='def'><b>Gerund</b>The <strong>-ing form</strong> of a verb used <strong>as a noun</strong>: <em><u>Swimming</u> is good for your health.</em> <em>I enjoy <u>reading</u>.</em></div><ul><li>A gerund can be the <strong>subject</strong> of a sentence: <em>Drawing is my hobby.</em></li><li>It can be the <strong>object</strong> of a verb: <em>I like dancing.</em></li><li>It can follow a <strong>preposition</strong>: <em>I am good at drawing.</em></li></ul><p class='formule'>gerund = base verb + -ing, used like a noun</p><p><strong>Spelling</strong>: <em>play → playing</em>, <em>read → reading</em>; drop the final -e: <em>dance → dancing</em>, <em>write → writing</em>; double the consonant after one short vowel: <em>swim → swimming</em>, <em>run → running</em>; -ie becomes -y: <em>lie → lying</em>.</p><div class='attention'><b>Watch out!</b>“I am swimming” is the present continuous (am + -ing), not a gerund. In “Swimming is fun”, swimming is a gerund: it is the subject, like a noun.</div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"Spelling the -ing form","legende":"Three spelling rules cover almost all the gerunds you need for the BEPC.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 200' role='img' aria-label='Three columns of spelling rules for the -ing form' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='200' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='200' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Base verb + -ing</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='142' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='112.66666666666667' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Add -ing</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>play → playing</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>read → reading</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>watch → watching</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ + ing</text><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='142' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#17784D' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#17784D'/><text x='320' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Drop the -e</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>dance → dancing</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>write → writing</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>ride → riding</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#17784D'>→ e disappears</text><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='142' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C2540A'/><text x='527.3333333333334' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Double</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>swim → swimming</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>run → running</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>shop → shopping</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C2540A'>→ double + ing</text><text x='634' y='195' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>First clue: in “Swim is my favourite activity”, the subject is an activity, so it must be a noun. English uses the gerund: “<strong>Swimming</strong> is my favourite activity.”</p>","verdicts":[[1,"rejetee","A verb in -ing can be the subject: Swimming is my favourite activity."]]},"retenir":"Gerund = verb + -ing used as a noun (subject, object, after a preposition)."},{"t":"Verbs followed by the gerund","verrou":true},{"t":"Gerunds after prepositions","verrou":true},{"t":"Vers le BEPC","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","c":"3e","m":"anglais","rang":36,"payant":true,"duree":35,"quiz":[],"apc":{"module":"Economic Life and Occupations","famille":"Vie économique","agir":"Communicate about economic life and occupations","situation":"Hamadou, 15, from Garoua, writes this profile to find a pen friend: “I enjoy to play football. I am interested in draw. Swim is my favourite activity. I want visiting Buea one day. I look forward to meet you!” His cousin says that five verbs are in the wrong form.","tache":"Correct the five verbs of Hamadou's profile and explain each correction."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
VRT_L("3e-anglais-question-tags",{"titre":"Question tags: checking information in a discussion on democracy","famille":"Citizenship and human rights","agir":"Check information and ask for agreement politely in a discussion","accroche":"“You are registered, isn't it?” French speakers add « n'est-ce pas ? » to everything. English has no single tag: it builds a new tag for each sentence.","intro":"In Bafoussam, Kamga and Nana attend a training course on democracy at the youth centre. Kamga's questions will teach you how to build question tags.","objectifs":["say what a question tag is and what it is used for","build a tag with the auxiliary and the subject pronoun","use do, does, did when the sentence has no auxiliary","use the special tags (I am, let's, imperatives, negative words) and the right intonation"],"enquete":{"titre":"The democracy course in Bafoussam","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='Two students in a meeting room in front of a ballot box and a board with the word democracy' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='qtC' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#E3ECF7'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F7F3EA'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#qtC)'/><rect y='186' width='640' height='34' fill='#C9A06E'/><rect x='230' y='30' width='180' height='70' fill='#fff' stroke='#9AA3AF'/><text x='320' y='58' text-anchor='middle' font-size='14' font-weight='700' fill='#1E499B'>DEMOCRACY</text><text x='320' y='80' text-anchor='middle' font-size='10' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>rights · duties · vote</text><rect x='280' y='120' width='80' height='60' fill='#DCE7F3' stroke='#4A6FA5'/><rect x='300' y='116' width='40' height='6' fill='#1F2328'/><rect x='306' y='104' width='28' height='14' fill='#fff' stroke='#9AA3AF'/><text x='320' y='156' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11' font-weight='700' fill='#1E499B'>VOTE</text><g transform='translate(130 96)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#6E1F1F'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#6E1F1F'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#C62828'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#C62828' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#C62828' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#5A3A1E'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/></g><g transform='translate(510 96)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#1E499B'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#3F2A18'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#3F2A18'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#3F2A18'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#3F2A18'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#3F2A18'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#3F2A18'/></g><rect x='20' y='26' width='230' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#F7C948'/><text x='135' y='46' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>You are registered, isn't it?</text><rect x='400' y='26' width='230' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#9FC5E8'/><text x='515' y='46' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Aren't you, Kamga!</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"In Bafoussam, young people take part in a training course on democracy at the youth centre.","contexte":"<p>During the course, Kamga asks his friend Nana a series of questions: “You are registered on the electoral list, isn't it? In Cameroon, we can vote at 20, isn't it? The course started yesterday, isn't it? Nobody voted twice, isn't it? Let's ask the facilitator, isn't it?” Nana laughs: “Kamga, you only know one tag! Each sentence needs its own.”</p>","documents":[{"t":"Facilitator's board","html":"<p>Voting is a right and a civic duty. In Cameroon, a citizen can register on the electoral list from the age of 20. Each voter votes only once, in secret, in a polling booth.</p>"}],"question":"How do we build the right question tag for each sentence?","tache":"Learn how question tags are built, then give each of Kamga's five questions its correct tag.","hypotheses":["“Isn't it?” works for every sentence, like « n'est-ce pas ? ».","The tag repeats the main verb of the sentence: “You like politics, like you?”","The tag uses the auxiliary of the sentence (or do, does, did) and the subject pronoun; a positive sentence takes a negative tag and a negative sentence a positive tag."]},"parties":[{"t":"What is a question tag?","html":"<div class='def'><b>Question tag</b>A short question added at the end of a statement to <strong>check information</strong> or to <strong>ask for agreement</strong>: <em>Voting is a right, <u>isn't it</u>?</em></div><p class='formule'>positive statement, negative tag? · negative statement, positive tag?</p><ul><li>The tag is made of an <strong>auxiliary</strong> (be, have, can, will, must…) + a <strong>subject pronoun</strong>.</li><li>The tag uses the <strong>same auxiliary</strong> and the <strong>same tense</strong> as the statement: <em>You <u>are</u> registered, <u>aren't</u> you?</em> <em>She <u>can</u> vote, <u>can't</u> she?</em> <em>They <u>will</u> come, <u>won't</u> they?</em></li><li>The negative tag is contracted: <em>isn't, aren't, wasn't, can't, won't, haven't</em>.</li></ul><div class='ex'><b>Example</b><em>Citizens have rights, <strong>haven't they</strong>?</em> · <em>You aren't tired, <strong>are you</strong>?</em> · <em>The facilitator was clear, <strong>wasn't he</strong>?</em></div><div class='attention'><b>French speakers, watch out!</b>English has no fixed tag like « n'est-ce pas ? ». <s>You are registered, isn't it?</s> → <em>You are registered, <strong>aren't you</strong>?</em></div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"Positive or negative?","legende":"The tag always takes the opposite form of the statement: positive → negative, negative → positive.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 200' role='img' aria-label='Two columns: positive statements with negative tags and negative statements with positive tags' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='200' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='200' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Same auxiliary, opposite form, subject pronoun</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='299' height='142' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='299' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='164.5' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Positive → negative tag</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>You are registered, aren't you?</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>She can vote, can't she?</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>They will come, won't they?</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ auxiliary + n't + pronoun</text><rect x='326' y='44' width='299' height='142' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#17784D' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='326' y='44' width='299' height='34' rx='11' fill='#17784D'/><text x='475.5' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Negative → positive tag</text><text x='336' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>You aren't tired, are you?</text><text x='336' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>He can't vote, can he?</text><text x='336' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>It wasn't long, was it?</text><text x='336' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#17784D'>→ auxiliary + pronoun</text><text x='634' y='195' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>First clue: “You are registered” uses <em>are</em> and the subject <em>you</em>, so the tag is “<strong>aren't you</strong>?”. “We can vote at 20” gives “<strong>can't we</strong>?”. <em>Isn't it</em> only fits a sentence with <em>is</em> and the subject <em>it</em>.</p>","verdicts":[[0,"rejetee","Each statement has its own tag; isn't it only follows a positive sentence with it is."]]},"retenir":"Tag = auxiliary of the sentence + subject pronoun; positive → negative tag, negative → positive tag."},{"t":"Tags with do, does and did","verrou":true,"illus":{"legende":"When there is no auxiliary. In the present simple and the past simple, do, does or did appear in the tag only.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 180' role='img' aria-label='Three columns: tags with do or does, with did, and with there' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='180' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='180' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>do, does, did and there</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='122' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='112.66666666666667' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Present simple</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>You vote, don't you?</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>He votes, doesn't he?</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ do / does</text><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='122' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C2540A'/><text x='320' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Past simple</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>It started, didn't it?</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>They left, didn't they?</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C2540A'>→ did</text><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='122' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#7B3F99'/><text x='527.3333333333334' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>There is / are</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>There is a booth,</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>isn't there?</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#7B3F99'>→ there, not it</text><text x='634' y='175' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}},{"t":"Special tags and intonation","verrou":true,"illus":{"legende":"Special cases. Learn these four special tags by heart: they appear often in the grammar section of the BEPC.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 180' role='img' aria-label='Three columns: special tags with I am and let's, with imperatives, and after negative words' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='180' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='180' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Special tags</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='122' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='112.66666666666667' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>I am / let's</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>I am late, aren't I?</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Let's go, shall we?</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ learn them</text><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='122' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C2540A'/><text x='320' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Imperative</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Sit down, will you?</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Help me, won't you?</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C2540A'>→ will / won't you</text><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='122' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#17784D' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#17784D'/><text x='527.3333333333334' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Negative words</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Nobody came, did they?</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>He never lies, does he?</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#17784D'>→ positive tag</text><text x='634' y='175' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}},{"t":"Vers le BEPC","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","c":"3e","m":"anglais","rang":83,"payant":true,"duree":35,"quiz":[],"apc":{"module":"Citizenship/Human Rights","famille":"Vie sociale et culturelle","agir":"Communicate about citizenship/human rights","situation":"During a training course on democracy in Bafoussam, Kamga asks: “You are registered on the electoral list, isn't it? In Cameroon, we can vote at 20, isn't it? The course started yesterday, isn't it? Nobody voted twice, isn't it? Let's ask the facilitator, isn't it?”","tache":"Give each of Kamga's five questions its correct tag and explain the rule you used."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
VRT_L("3e-anglais-phrasal-verbs",{"titre":"Phrasal verbs: campaigning and voting for school prefects","famille":"Citizenship and human rights","agir":"Talk about an election campaign and its stages","accroche":"“I will never give!” shouts Ebai at the end of his campaign speech. His schoolmates laugh: give what? He meant “give up”, and one small word changes everything.","intro":"In Kumba, Ebai is a candidate for senior prefect. His campaign speech will show you what phrasal verbs are and how to use them.","objectifs":["say what a phrasal verb is","understand that the particle changes the meaning of the verb","use the phrasal verbs of an election campaign","place a pronoun object correctly (put them up, look after them)"],"enquete":{"titre":"Ebai's campaign speech","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='A student candidate speaks in a school yard in front of a notice board covered with campaign posters' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='pvC' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#E4F0E4'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F7F3EA'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#pvC)'/><rect y='186' width='640' height='34' fill='#C9A06E'/><rect x='230' y='40' width='180' height='110' fill='#8A5A2B'/><rect x='240' y='50' width='50' height='40' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B'/><text x='265' y='74' text-anchor='middle' font-size='10' font-weight='700' fill='#1E499B'>VOTE</text><rect x='296' y='50' width='50' height='40' fill='#fff' stroke='#C62828'/><text x='321' y='74' text-anchor='middle' font-size='10' font-weight='700' fill='#C62828'>EBAI</text><rect x='352' y='50' width='50' height='40' fill='#fff' stroke='#17784D'/><text x='377' y='74' text-anchor='middle' font-size='10' font-weight='700' fill='#17784D'>FOR</text><rect x='262' y='100' width='116' height='40' fill='#FFF6D6' stroke='#C9A04A'/><text x='320' y='124' text-anchor='middle' font-size='10' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>ELECTION DAY</text><rect x='316' y='150' width='8' height='36' fill='#5C3D22'/><g transform='translate(130 96)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#1F2328'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#1E499B'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2F1A'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2F1A'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#4A2F1A'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#4A2F1A'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2F1A'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2F1A'/></g><g transform='translate(510 96)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#17784D'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#17784D' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#17784D' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#6B4423'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#6B4423'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#6B4423'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#6B4423'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#6B4423'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#6B4423'/></g><rect x='20' y='26' width='230' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#F7C948'/><text x='135' y='46' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>I will never give!</text><rect x='400' y='26' width='230' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#9FC5E8'/><text x='515' y='46' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Never give… what?</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"In a secondary school in Kumba, Ebai presents his programme to become senior prefect.","contexte":"<p>Ebai's draft speech says: “Dear schoolmates, I have decided to be candidate in this election. Tomorrow I will fix my posters on the walls. If you elect me, I will look the problems of every student and I will make my promises. I will never give! Please come on election day and vote me!” His friend Mbah reads it: “Your programme is good, but English speakers will not understand half of it. You need phrasal verbs.”</p>","documents":[{"t":"Election calendar posted by the principal","html":"<p>Monday: candidates hand in their applications. Tuesday to Thursday: campaign; posters only on the notice boards. Friday: voting from 8 a.m. to noon; results in the afternoon.</p>"}],"question":"What are phrasal verbs, and how can Ebai use them in his speech?","tache":"Learn what phrasal verbs are and how they work, then rewrite Ebai's speech with six correct phrasal verbs.","hypotheses":["A phrasal verb means exactly the verb plus the particle: give up = give + up, to give upwards.","The particle is not important: look, look for, look after and look into mean the same.","A phrasal verb is a verb + particle with its own meaning; with a pronoun object, a separable phrasal verb puts the pronoun in the middle (put them up)."]},"parties":[{"t":"What is a phrasal verb?","html":"<div class='def'><b>Phrasal verb</b>A verb followed by a <strong>particle</strong> (an adverb or a preposition: up, down, in, out, on, off, for, after, into…). Together, they form a <strong>new meaning</strong>: <em>give up</em> = stop trying.</div><ul><li>Sometimes the meaning is <strong>literal</strong>: <em>stand up</em> (se lever), <em>sit down</em>, <em>go out</em>.</li><li>Most of the time it is <strong>idiomatic</strong>: you cannot guess it from the verb: <em>give up</em> (abandon), <em>turn up</em> (arrive, come), <em>carry out</em> (do, perform).</li><li>The <strong>particle changes the meaning</strong>: <em>look <u>for</u></em> (search), <em>look <u>after</u></em> (take care of), <em>look <u>into</u></em> (examine).</li></ul><p class='formule'>phrasal verb = verb + particle = a new meaning</p><div class='ex'><b>Example</b><em>Ebai will look <strong>into</strong> the students' problems</em> (he will examine them). <em>The prefect looks <strong>after</strong> the younger students</em> (he takes care of them).</div><div class='attention'><b>Watch out!</b>Do not drop the particle: <s>I will never give!</s> → <em>I will never <strong>give up</strong>!</em> Without up, give needs an object (give something).</div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"One verb, three meanings","legende":"With look, the particle decides the meaning: you must learn each phrasal verb as a new word.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 200' role='img' aria-label='Three columns: look for, look after and look into, with their meanings' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='200' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='200' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>look + particle</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='142' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='112.66666666666667' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>look for</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>search, try to find</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>I am looking for my</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>voter's card.</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ chercher</text><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='142' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#17784D' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#17784D'/><text x='320' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>look after</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>take care of</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>The prefect looks after</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>the young students.</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#17784D'>→ s'occuper de</text><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='142' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C2540A'/><text x='527.3333333333334' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>look into</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>examine, study</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>I will look into</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>your complaints.</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C2540A'>→ examiner</text><text x='634' y='195' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>First clue: <em>give up</em> does not mean “give upwards”: it means <strong>stop trying</strong>. Ebai must write “I will never <strong>give up</strong>!” The particle carries part of the meaning.</p>","verdicts":[[0,"rejetee","A phrasal verb has its own meaning: give up = stop trying, not give + up."]]},"retenir":"Phrasal verb = verb + particle with a new meaning; the particle changes the meaning (look for / after / into)."},{"t":"Phrasal verbs for an election campaign","verrou":true},{"t":"Word order: separable and inseparable","verrou":true},{"t":"Vers le BEPC","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","c":"3e","m":"anglais","rang":88,"payant":true,"duree":35,"quiz":[],"apc":{"module":"Citizenship/Human Rights","famille":"Vie sociale et culturelle","agir":"Communicate about citizenship/human rights","situation":"Ebai, a candidate for senior prefect in Kumba, wrote: “I have decided to be candidate in this election. Tomorrow I will fix my posters on the walls. If you elect me, I will look the problems of every student and I will make my promises. I will never give! Please come on election day and vote me!”","tache":"Rewrite Ebai's speech with six correct phrasal verbs, then explain the meaning of two of them."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
