VRT_L("3e-anglais-listening-neighbours-religions",{"titre":"Listening: socialising with neighbours of other religions","duree":35,"famille":"Family and social life","agir":"Listen to a conversation between neighbours of different religions, identify the information and the attitudes, and react politely","accroche":"In Ngaoundéré, the Christian family of Grace has just moved next to the Muslim family of Alhadji Bouba. On Friday, Bouba's son Moussa knocks at the door with a plate of food. Grace's little brother says: “Don't eat it, it's not our religion!” What should Grace answer?","intro":"Grace and her new neighbour Moussa live side by side in Ngaoundéré, in families of different religions. Their conversation will help you learn the vocabulary of religions and neighbourhood life, and the strategies to listen to a dialogue and understand both the facts and the feelings.","objectifs":["use the vocabulary of religions and neighbourhood life: church, mosque, prayer, feast, fasting, neighbour, to invite, to share, to respect","listen to a dialogue for the main idea, the details and the speakers' attitudes","recognise polite and friendly expressions: You're welcome, Thank you for…, Would you like to…?","react respectfully to people of other religions"],"enquete":{"titre":"A plate from next door","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='Two neighbours at a door, one offering a plate of food, with a church and a mosque in the background' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='vsC' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#E8F5E9'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F7F3EA'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#vsC)'/><rect y='176' width='640' height='44' fill='#D7CCC8'/><rect x='430' y='70' width='70' height='106' fill='#ECEFF1'/><rect x='460' y='30' width='8' height='44' fill='#ECEFF1'/><rect x='452' y='40' width='24' height='6' fill='#5D4037'/><rect x='530' y='90' width='80' height='86' fill='#FFF8E1'/><circle cx='570' cy='88' r='24' fill='#43A047'/><rect x='200' y='70' width='70' height='106' fill='#8D6E63'/><g transform='translate(160 92)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#C2540A'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#5A3A1E'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/></g><g transform='translate(310 92)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#1E499B'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#4A2E1A'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/></g><ellipse cx='292' cy='132' rx='16' ry='5' fill='#FFB74D'/><rect x='20' y='20' width='300' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#A5D6A7'/><text x='170' y='40' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>My mother sent you some food…</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"In Ngaoundéré, Moussa brings a plate of food to his new Christian neighbours.","contexte":"<p>Grace's little brother Paul refuses the food: “It's not our religion!” Grace hesitates. Her English class has recorded a conversation between two neighbours and asks the pupils to listen to it and answer questions on the facts and on the speakers' attitudes. Grace listens once and only hears “feast”, “Friday” and “thank you”. In the neighbourhood live about 40 families: 22 Muslim and 18 Christian.</p>","documents":[{"t":"The recorded conversation (transcript)","html":"<p><strong>Moussa</strong>: “Good evening! I'm Moussa, from next door. Today is the end of Ramadan, our big feast. My mother sent you some food to welcome you to the neighbourhood.” — <strong>Grace</strong>: “Oh, thank you so much! That's very kind of you. Please thank your mother for us.” — <strong>Moussa</strong>: “You're welcome. Is it true that you celebrate Christmas in December?” — <strong>Grace</strong>: “Yes, on the 25th. Would you like to come and eat with us? You can bring your sisters.” — <strong>Moussa</strong>: “With pleasure! In our neighbourhood, we always share our feasts.”</p>"}],"question":"How do we listen to a conversation between neighbours and understand both the facts and the feelings?","tache":"Learn the vocabulary of religions and neighbourhood life and the listening strategies, then answer the questions on the conversation and say how Grace should react.","hypotheses":["Neighbours of another religion should not share food or feasts.","Hearing a few words (feast, Friday, thank you) is enough to understand the conversation.","We listen for the main idea, the details and the polite expressions that show the speakers' attitudes, then we react with respect."]},"parties":[{"t":"The vocabulary of religions and neighbourhood life","html":"<div class='def'><b>Religious tolerance</b>Respecting people whose religion is different from ours: accepting their beliefs, their places of worship and their feasts, and living peacefully with them.</div><ul><li><strong>Places</strong>: <em>a church, a mosque, a temple, a sacred forest, a place of worship</em>.</li><li><strong>Practices</strong>: <em>to pray, a prayer, fasting (Ramadan, Lent), a feast, a pilgrimage, a sermon</em>.</li><li><strong>People</strong>: <em>a Christian, a Muslim, a believer, a pastor, a priest, an imam, a neighbour</em>.</li><li><strong>Socialising</strong>: <em>to welcome, to invite, to share a meal, to visit, to greet, to wish someone a happy feast</em>.</li><li><strong>Attitudes</strong>: <em>respect, kindness, friendship, prejudice, to accept, to reject</em>.</li></ul><p class='formule'>different beliefs + respect + sharing = good neighbourliness</p><div class='ex'><b>Words in context</b><em>Every year, our Muslim neighbours invite us for the end of Ramadan, and we invite them for Christmas. We wish each other a happy feast.</em></div><div class='attention'><b>Attention</b>“Feast” is a religious or traditional celebration; “party” is an ordinary celebration. Say <em>a happy feast</em> or <em>Eid Mubarak</em>, <em>Merry Christmas</em>.</div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"Two religions, one neighbourhood","legende":"Different places and feasts, the same gestures of friendship.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='Three columns: Christians, Muslims and neighbours' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Living together</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='162' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='112.66666666666667' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Christians</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>church, pastor, priest</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Sunday service</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Christmas, Easter</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ Merry Christmas!</text><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='162' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='320' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Muslims</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>mosque, imam</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Friday prayer</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>end of Ramadan, Tabaski</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ Eid Mubarak!</text><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='162' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C2540A'/><text x='527.3333333333334' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Neighbours</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>greet, visit</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>share a meal</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>help each other</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C2540A'>→ respect</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>Paul is wrong: sharing food with a neighbour is not changing religion. In Cameroon, many families of different religions share their feasts: it is a sign of respect and friendship, not a betrayal of one's faith.</p>","verdicts":[[0,"rejetee","Sharing a meal with neighbours of another religion is a sign of respect, not a betrayal."]]},"retenir":"church, mosque, prayer, feast, fasting ; to welcome, to invite, to share ; respect, kindness, prejudice."},{"t":"Listening for facts and feelings","verrou":true},{"t":"Reacting with respect","verrou":true},{"t":"Vers le BEPC","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","c":"3e","rang":4,"m":"anglais","payant":true,"quiz":[],"apc":{"module":"Family and Social Life","famille":"Vie familiale et sociale","agir":"Communicate about family and social life","situation":"In Ngaoundéré, Moussa, a Muslim neighbour, brings food to Grace's Christian family for the end of Ramadan. Grace's little brother refuses because “it's not our religion”, and Grace, listening to a recorded conversation, only catches “feast, Friday, thank you”.","tache":"Learn the vocabulary of religions and neighbourhood life and the listening strategies, then answer the questions on the conversation and say how Grace should react."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
VRT_L("3e-anglais-reading-tolerance",{"titre":"Reading: tolerating and accepting others","duree":35,"famille":"Family and social life","agir":"Read a text about tolerance, find the main idea and the details, and give a personal reaction","accroche":"In a school in Bafoussam, a new pupil, Ibrahim, arrives in a wheelchair. Some classmates laugh at him; others look away. Then the class reads a text about tolerance. Can a text change what we think of others?","intro":"The Form 4 pupils of a school in Bafoussam read a text about tolerance after the arrival of Ibrahim, a pupil in a wheelchair. Their reading will help you learn the vocabulary of tolerance and the strategies to find the main idea, the details and the writer's message.","objectifs":["use the vocabulary of tolerance: to accept, to respect, to tease, to exclude, disability, differences, empathy, discrimination","find the main idea of each paragraph (topic sentence)","answer comprehension questions with quotations from the text","give a personal reaction: I think the writer is right because…"],"enquete":{"titre":"Ibrahim's first week","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='A classroom with a pupil in a wheelchair, some pupils laughing and one helping' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='tlC' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#EDE7F6'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F7F3EA'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#tlC)'/><rect y='176' width='640' height='44' fill='#D7CCC8'/><rect x='380' y='40' width='220' height='80' fill='#2E4A3A'/><text x='490' y='86' text-anchor='middle' font-size='14' font-weight='700' fill='#FAFAFA'>TOLERANCE</text><circle cx='120' cy='168' r='18' fill='none' stroke='#37474F' stroke-width='4'/><g transform='translate(120 82)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#C2540A'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#4A2E1A'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/></g><g transform='translate(200 92)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#2E7D32'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#5A3A1E'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/></g><g transform='translate(300 92)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#7B3F99'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#6B4423'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#6B4423'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#6B4423'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#6B4423'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#6B4423'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#6B4423'/></g><rect x='20' y='20' width='280' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#B39DDB'/><text x='160' y='40' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Can I help you with your bag?</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"In Bafoussam, Ibrahim arrives in a wheelchair; his classmates read a text about tolerance.","contexte":"<p>During the first week, some pupils tease Ibrahim, and nobody sits next to him. Their teacher gives them a text, “Different, but equal”, and three questions. Florence says: “A text is just words: you read it, you answer, and nothing changes.” Junior reads only the first line and answers the questions with his own opinion. In the class, 3 pupils out of 45 have a disability or a chronic illness.</p>","documents":[{"t":"The text: “Different, but equal”","html":"<p>(1) Every person is different: we have different faces, languages, religions, abilities and ideas. These differences are not a problem; they are a richness. — (2) Tolerance means accepting people as they are and respecting their rights, even when they are not like us. A tolerant person does not tease, insult or exclude others because of their disability, their ethnic group or their religion. — (3) Intolerance can hurt deeply. A pupil who is excluded may feel lonely, lose confidence and leave school. — (4) Each of us can act: say hello to a new pupil, invite him or her to play, defend a classmate who is teased. As the proverb says, “One finger cannot pick up a stone.”</p>"}],"question":"How do we read a text about tolerance to understand its message and react to it?","tache":"Learn the vocabulary of tolerance and the reading strategies, then answer the questions on the text and write a short personal reaction.","hypotheses":["A text is just words: it cannot change our attitudes.","Reading the first line and answering with our own opinion is enough.","We find the main idea of each paragraph, quote the text to answer, then give a personal reaction linked to our life."]},"parties":[{"t":"The vocabulary of tolerance","html":"<div class='def'><b>Tolerance</b>The attitude of accepting people who are different from us (in appearance, ability, language, ethnic group or religion) and respecting their rights and their dignity.</div><ul><li><strong>Positive attitudes</strong>: <em>to accept, to respect, to include, to welcome, to help, to defend, empathy, kindness</em>.</li><li><strong>Negative attitudes</strong>: <em>to tease, to mock, to insult, to exclude, to bully, discrimination, intolerance, prejudice</em>.</li><li><strong>Differences</strong>: <em>a disability, a wheelchair, an ethnic group, a religion, a language, an accent, a skin colour</em>.</li><li><strong>Feelings</strong>: <em>lonely, hurt, ashamed, confident, accepted, proud</em>.</li></ul><p class='formule'>differences + respect = tolerance ; differences + rejection = intolerance</p><div class='ex'><b>Words in context</b><em>Empathy is putting yourself in someone else's shoes: imagine how Ibrahim feels when people laugh at him.</em></div><div class='attention'><b>Attention</b>“To tolerate” is not only “to support” (supporter) something unpleasant; in this lesson, tolerance means real acceptance and respect.</div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"Tolerance or intolerance?","legende":"The same difference can lead to two attitudes, with opposite effects on the person.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='Two columns comparing intolerance and tolerance' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Two attitudes</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='299' height='162' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C62828' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='299' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C62828'/><text x='164.5' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Intolerance</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>tease, mock</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>exclude, insult</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>prejudice</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C62828'>→ lonely, hurt</text><rect x='326' y='44' width='299' height='162' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='326' y='44' width='299' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='475.5' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Tolerance</text><text x='336' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>accept, respect</text><text x='336' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>include, help</text><text x='336' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>empathy</text><text x='336' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ confident, proud</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>Florence is wrong: a text can change attitudes because it makes us think and puts words on what we see. After reading paragraph 3, the class understands that teasing can make a pupil lonely and leave school.</p>","verdicts":[[0,"rejetee","A text can change attitudes: it makes us think about what we do."]]},"retenir":"to accept, to respect, to include ; to tease, to exclude, discrimination ; disability ; empathy."},{"t":"Finding the main idea and the details","verrou":true,"illus":{"legende":"The plan of the text. Each paragraph has one main idea, given by its first sentence.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='Four columns: the main idea of each paragraph' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>“Different, but equal”</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='143.5' height='162' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='143.5' height='34' rx='11' fill='#7B3F99'/><text x='86.75' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>§1</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>everybody is different</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>differences</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>= richness</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='800' fill='#7B3F99'>→ idea</text><rect x='170.5' y='44' width='143.5' height='162' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='170.5' y='44' width='143.5' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='242.25' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>§2</text><text x='180.5' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>definition</text><text x='180.5' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>accept, respect</text><text x='180.5' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>no exclusion</text><text x='180.5' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ definition</text><rect x='326' y='44' width='143.5' height='162' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C62828' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='326' y='44' width='143.5' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C62828'/><text x='397.75' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>§3</text><text x='336' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>intolerance hurts</text><text x='336' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>lonely</text><text x='336' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>leave school</text><text x='336' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C62828'>→ consequence</text><rect x='481.5' y='44' width='143.5' height='162' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='481.5' y='44' width='143.5' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='553.25' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>§4</text><text x='491.5' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>each of us can act</text><text x='491.5' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>say hello, invite</text><text x='491.5' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>defend</text><text x='491.5' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ message</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}},{"t":"Giving a personal reaction","verrou":true},{"t":"Vers le BEPC","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","c":"3e","rang":7,"m":"anglais","payant":true,"quiz":[],"apc":{"module":"Family and Social Life","famille":"Vie familiale et sociale","agir":"Communicate about family and social life","situation":"In a school in Bafoussam, Ibrahim, a new pupil in a wheelchair, is teased and left alone. The class reads a text, “Different, but equal”, but Florence thinks a text changes nothing and Junior answers after reading only the first line.","tache":"Learn the vocabulary of tolerance and the reading strategies, then answer the questions on the text and write a short personal reaction."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
VRT_L("3e-anglais-speaking-gender-equality",{"titre":"Speaking: volunteering for gender equality","duree":35,"famille":"Citizenship and human rights","agir":"Exchange information and opinions about volunteering in activities that promote equality between girls and boys","accroche":"In a village near Bertoua, many girls leave school at 14 to help at home or to marry. The youth club wants to start a homework group for girls. Thierry says: “Volunteering is for girls, and school is more important for boys anyway.” His sister Mireille disagrees. How do we discuss gender equality in English?","intro":"The youth club of a village near Bertoua wants to help girls stay at school. The members' discussion will help you learn the vocabulary of gender equality and volunteering, and the expressions to ask for and give information, opinions and proposals.","objectifs":["use the vocabulary of gender equality and volunteering: equal rights, gender, chores, early marriage, to volunteer, to campaign, to raise awareness","ask for and give information: How many…? What can we do? Who will…?","express opinions and react: I strongly believe…, I partly agree…, That's not fair!","propose and volunteer: I'd like to help with…, I can…, Count me in!"],"enquete":{"titre":"The homework group","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='A village youth club: boys and girls around a table with notebooks, a banner Equal chances' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='egC' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#F3E5F5'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F7F3EA'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#egC)'/><rect y='176' width='640' height='44' fill='#DCEDC8'/><rect x='360' y='34' width='250' height='36' rx='6' fill='#7B3F99'/><text x='485' y='58' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>EQUAL CHANCES FOR ALL</text><rect x='370' y='130' width='200' height='12' fill='#8D6E63'/><g transform='translate(90 92)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#7B3F99'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#5A3A1E'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/></g><g transform='translate(160 92)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#1E499B'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#4A2E1A'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/></g><g transform='translate(230 92)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#C2540A'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#6B4423'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#6B4423'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#6B4423'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#6B4423'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#6B4423'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#6B4423'/></g><g transform='translate(300 92)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#2E7D32'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#4A2E1A'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/></g><rect x='20' y='14' width='300' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#CE93D8'/><text x='170' y='34' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>I'd like to help with maths!</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"Near Bertoua, the youth club plans a homework group to help girls stay at school.","contexte":"<p>Thierry thinks volunteering and equality are “girls' business”. Another member, Désiré, just says: “Equality is good. OK. Next topic.” Their leader asks each member to give one piece of information, one opinion with a reason and one proposal. The club's survey shows that in the village school, there are 60 girls and 60 boys in Form 1, but only 15 girls and 40 boys in Form 5.</p>","documents":[{"t":"The club's survey","html":"<p>Form 1: 60 girls, 60 boys · Form 5: 15 girls, 40 boys · Reasons why girls leave: household chores (water, cooking, younger children), early marriage, no money for fees, no time to study · Ideas: a homework group twice a week, sharing chores between boys and girls at home, talks with parents, a mentor for each girl.</p>"}],"question":"How do we exchange information and opinions about volunteering for gender equality?","tache":"Learn the vocabulary of gender equality and volunteering and the language of discussion, then act out the club's meeting and agree on volunteers' tasks.","hypotheses":["Gender equality is only the business of girls.","Saying “Equality is good” is enough to take part in the discussion.","Each member gives information from the survey, an opinion with a reason and a concrete proposal to volunteer."]},"parties":[{"t":"The vocabulary of gender equality and volunteering","html":"<div class='def'><b>Gender equality</b>The principle that girls and boys, women and men, have the same rights, the same opportunities and the same responsibilities: at school, at home, at work and in public life.</div><ul><li><strong>Rights</strong>: <em>equal rights, the right to education, equal opportunities, to be treated fairly</em>.</li><li><strong>Problems</strong>: <em>discrimination, early marriage, school dropout, household chores, stereotypes</em>.</li><li><strong>Volunteering</strong>: <em>a volunteer, to volunteer, a campaign, to campaign, to raise awareness, a mentor, to support, to encourage</em>.</li><li><strong>Activities</strong>: <em>a homework group, a talk, a debate, a poster, a sketch, a mentoring programme</em>.</li></ul><p class='formule'>same rights + same opportunities + shared responsibilities = gender equality</p><div class='ex'><b>Words in context</b><em>A volunteer gives his or her time without being paid. In our club, boys and girls volunteer to help girls with their homework.</em></div><div class='attention'><b>Attention</b>“Gender” refers to the roles society gives to girls and boys; “sex” is biological. A “stereotype” is a fixed idea: “Cooking is for girls.”</div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"From problem to action","legende":"The club links each problem found in the survey to a volunteer action.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='Three columns: problem, action and volunteers' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Helping girls stay at school</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='162' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C62828' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C62828'/><text x='112.66666666666667' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Problem</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>chores at home</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>early marriage</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>no study time</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C62828'>→ dropout</text><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='162' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='320' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Action</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>share chores</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>talk to parents</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>homework group</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ support</text><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='162' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='527.3333333333334' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Volunteers</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>boys and girls</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>mentors</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>teachers</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ together</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>Thierry is wrong: gender equality concerns everybody. Boys can share household chores, encourage their sisters and volunteer as tutors. Equality is built by girls and boys together.</p>","verdicts":[[0,"rejetee","Gender equality concerns girls and boys: everybody can volunteer."]]},"retenir":"equal rights, opportunities ; discrimination, stereotype, early marriage, dropout ; volunteer, campaign, mentor, raise awareness."},{"t":"Asking for and giving information and opinions","verrou":true,"illus":{"legende":"Girls and boys in the village school. The figures of the survey: in Form 1, as many girls as boys; in Form 5, far fewer girls.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='Three columns: girls, boys and the reasons for dropout' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Form 1 → Form 5</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='162' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#7B3F99'/><text x='112.66666666666667' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Girls</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Form 1: 60</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Form 5: 15</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>lost: 45</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#7B3F99'>→ 75 % leave</text><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='162' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='320' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Boys</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Form 1: 60</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Form 5: 40</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>lost: 20</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ 33 % leave</text><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='162' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C2540A'/><text x='527.3333333333334' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Why?</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>chores</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>early marriage</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>fees</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C2540A'>→ act!</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}},{"t":"Volunteering and sharing tasks","verrou":true},{"t":"Vers le BEPC","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","c":"3e","rang":79,"m":"anglais","payant":true,"quiz":[],"apc":{"module":"Citizenship/Human Rights","famille":"Citoyenneté","agir":"Communicate about citizenship and human rights","situation":"Near Bertoua, the village school has 60 girls in Form 1 but only 15 in Form 5. In the youth club, Thierry says equality is girls' business and Désiré only says “Equality is good. OK.”","tache":"Learn the vocabulary of gender equality and volunteering and the language of discussion, then act out the club's meeting and agree on volunteers' tasks."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
VRT_L("3e-anglais-reading-polls-surveys",{"titre":"Reading: taking part in polls and surveys","duree":35,"famille":"Citizenship and human rights","agir":"Read a questionnaire and the results of a survey, understand the figures and answer questions on them","accroche":"The student council of a school in Limbe asks every pupil to fill in a questionnaire on the school canteen. Elvis ticks answers at random without reading the questions, and his friend Joy says: “Surveys are useless, nobody reads them.” Who is right?","intro":"The student council of a school in Limbe organises a survey on the canteen. Its questionnaire and its results will help you learn the vocabulary of polls and surveys and the strategies to read questions, charts and percentages.","objectifs":["use the vocabulary of polls and surveys: a questionnaire, a respondent, a sample, results, a majority, a percentage, a chart, to tick, to rate","read a questionnaire carefully: closed questions, open questions, rating scales","read the results of a survey: percentages, majority, minority, comparisons","explain why taking part in a survey is a form of citizenship"],"enquete":{"titre":"The canteen survey","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='A pupil filling in a questionnaire, a box for answers and a bar chart of results' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='sdC' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#E3F2FD'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F7F3EA'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#sdC)'/><rect y='176' width='640' height='44' fill='#ECEFF1'/><rect x='400' y='120' width='40' height='56' fill='#1E499B'/><rect x='450' y='70' width='40' height='106' fill='#2E7D32'/><rect x='500' y='140' width='40' height='36' fill='#C2540A'/><rect x='550' y='150' width='40' height='26' fill='#7B3F99'/><path d='M390 176H600' stroke='#001136'/><g transform='translate(130 92)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#1E499B'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#4A2E1A'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/></g><rect x='150' y='110' width='40' height='52' fill='#fff' stroke='#9AA3AF'/><path d='M156 122h28M156 134h28M156 146h28' stroke='#9AA3AF'/><rect x='240' y='130' width='60' height='46' fill='#FFF8E1' stroke='#C9A04A'/><rect x='20' y='20' width='300' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#90CAF9'/><text x='170' y='40' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Please tick one answer only.</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"In Limbe, the student council collects pupils' opinions on the canteen with a questionnaire.","contexte":"<p>Elvis ticks answers without reading, and ticks two boxes where only one is allowed. Joy thinks surveys are useless. The council has received 400 questionnaires out of 500 pupils. The principal will use the results to decide what to change in the canteen next term.</p>","documents":[{"t":"Questionnaire and results","html":"<p><strong>Q1</strong> (tick one answer only): How often do you eat at the canteen? ☐ every day ☐ 2–3 times a week ☐ never. <strong>Q2</strong>: Rate the food from 1 (very bad) to 5 (excellent). <strong>Q3</strong> (open question): What would you change? — <strong>Results (400 respondents)</strong>: every day 50 % · 2–3 times a week 30 % · never 20 %. Average rating: 2.8 / 5. Main suggestions: lower prices (45 %), more vegetables (25 %), shorter queue (20 %), other (10 %).</p>"}],"question":"How do we read a questionnaire and the results of a survey?","tache":"Learn the vocabulary of polls and surveys and the reading strategies, then answer Elvis's questionnaire correctly and explain the results to Joy.","hypotheses":["We can tick answers at random: one questionnaire does not change anything.","Surveys are useless because nobody reads the results.","We read each question and its instructions, answer honestly, and we read the results with their percentages to understand what most people think."]},"parties":[{"t":"The vocabulary of polls and surveys","html":"<div class='def'><b>Survey</b>A study in which a group of people (the respondents) answer the same questions, so that we can know their opinions or habits. A poll is a short survey, often about one question or an election.</div><ul><li><strong>Documents</strong>: <em>a questionnaire, a form, a question, an answer, a box, a chart, a table</em>.</li><li><strong>People</strong>: <em>a respondent, an interviewer, a sample (a group chosen to represent everybody)</em>.</li><li><strong>Results</strong>: <em>a percentage, a majority, a minority, an average, a rating</em>.</li><li><strong>Verbs</strong>: <em>to fill in, to tick, to circle, to rate, to answer, to collect, to analyse</em>.</li><li><strong>Question types</strong>: <em>closed question (yes / no, choices), open question (free answer), rating scale (1 to 5)</em>.</li></ul><p class='formule'>questionnaire → respondents → results → decision</p><div class='ex'><b>Instructions of a questionnaire</b><em>Please fill in this questionnaire. Tick one box only. Your answers are anonymous: nobody will know who wrote them.</em></div><div class='attention'><b>Attention</b>“Anonymous” means without the name of the person: in an anonymous survey, you can give your true opinion freely.</div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"Three kinds of questions","legende":"A questionnaire mixes closed questions, rating scales and open questions.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='Three columns: closed questions, rating scales and open questions' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Reading the questions</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='162' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='112.66666666666667' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Closed</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>yes / no</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>tick one box</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>every day / never</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ quick to count</text><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='162' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C2540A'/><text x='320' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Rating scale</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>from 1 to 5</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>very bad → excellent</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>circle a number</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C2540A'>→ an average</text><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='162' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='527.3333333333334' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Open</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>What would you…?</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>free answer</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>your own words</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ ideas</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>Elvis is wrong: if many pupils tick at random, the results become false, and the principal may take bad decisions. And a questionnaire with two boxes ticked where only one was allowed cannot be counted: his opinion is lost.</p>","verdicts":[[0,"rejetee","Random or wrong answers make the results false and the opinion is lost."]]},"retenir":"questionnaire, respondent, sample ; percentage, majority, average ; to fill in, to tick, to rate ; anonymous."},{"t":"Reading the results","verrou":true,"illus":{"legende":"The results in figures. Percentages of the 400 respondents, and the numbers of pupils they represent.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 210' role='img' aria-label='Four columns: suggestions with percentages and numbers' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Main suggestions</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='143.5' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C62828' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='143.5' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C62828'/><text x='86.75' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Lower prices</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>45 %</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>180 pupils</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C62828'>→ the first</text><rect x='170.5' y='44' width='143.5' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='170.5' y='44' width='143.5' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='242.25' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>More vegetables</text><text x='180.5' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>25 %</text><text x='180.5' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>100 pupils</text><text x='180.5' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ second</text><rect x='326' y='44' width='143.5' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='326' y='44' width='143.5' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='397.75' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Shorter queue</text><text x='336' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>20 %</text><text x='336' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>80 pupils</text><text x='336' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ third</text><rect x='481.5' y='44' width='143.5' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='481.5' y='44' width='143.5' height='34' rx='11' fill='#7B3F99'/><text x='553.25' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Other</text><text x='491.5' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>10 %</text><text x='491.5' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>40 pupils</text><text x='491.5' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='800' fill='#7B3F99'>→ various</text><text x='634' y='205' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}},{"t":"Why take part in surveys?","verrou":true},{"t":"Vers le BEPC","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","c":"3e","rang":85,"m":"anglais","payant":true,"quiz":[],"apc":{"module":"Citizenship/Human Rights","famille":"Citoyenneté","agir":"Communicate about citizenship and human rights","situation":"In a school in Limbe, the student council organises a survey on the canteen: 400 questionnaires out of 500 come back. Elvis ticks answers at random and ticks two boxes where only one is allowed, and Joy says surveys are useless.","tache":"Learn the vocabulary of polls and surveys and the reading strategies, then answer Elvis's questionnaire correctly and explain the results to Joy."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
VRT_L("3e-anglais-speaking-service-packages",{"titre":"Speaking: subscribing to a phone or internet package","duree":35,"famille":"Media and communication","agir":"Ask for information about phone and internet packages, compare them and subscribe to the one that suits you","accroche":"In Bamenda, Ngwa needs internet for his online revision course: about 6 GB a month. In the phone shop, he points at a poster and says: “That one!” Two weeks later, he has no data left. How do we ask the right questions in English before subscribing?","intro":"Ngwa, a pupil in Bamenda, wants to subscribe to an internet package for his revision. His visit to the phone shop will help you learn the vocabulary of phone and internet services and the expressions to ask for information, compare offers and subscribe.","objectifs":["use the vocabulary of phone and internet services: a package (bundle), data, GB, airtime, validity, to subscribe, to top up, to renew, network coverage","ask for information: How much does it cost? How long is it valid? How much data do I get?","compare offers and justify a choice: cheaper per GB, longer validity","subscribe and confirm politely: I'd like to subscribe to…, Could you activate it, please?"],"enquete":{"titre":"Ngwa in the phone shop","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='A phone shop with a board of three internet packages, a shop assistant and a boy with a phone' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='fbC' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#FFFDE7'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F7F3EA'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#fbC)'/><rect y='176' width='640' height='44' fill='#CFD8DC'/><rect x='360' y='30' width='250' height='100' rx='8' fill='#FAFAFA' stroke='#9AA3AF'/><rect x='372' y='44' width='70' height='74' fill='#1E499B'/><rect x='450' y='44' width='70' height='74' fill='#2E7D32'/><rect x='528' y='44' width='70' height='74' fill='#C62828'/><text x='407' y='86' text-anchor='middle' font-size='18' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>A</text><text x='485' y='86' text-anchor='middle' font-size='18' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>B</text><text x='563' y='86' text-anchor='middle' font-size='18' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>C</text><rect x='330' y='140' width='280' height='36' fill='#F9A825'/><g transform='translate(130 92)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#7B3F99'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#5A3A1E'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/></g><rect x='146' y='100' width='8' height='14' rx='2' fill='#263238'/><rect x='20' y='20' width='300' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#FFF59D'/><text x='170' y='40' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>How long is this package valid?</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"In Bamenda, Ngwa compares three internet packages before subscribing.","contexte":"<p>Ngwa chooses the first package he sees, without asking anything. His cousin Sandra says: “Always take the cheapest one!” The shop assistant explains that a good customer asks about the price, the data, the validity and the network coverage, then compares. Ngwa needs about 6 GB a month and has a budget of 5 000 FCFA.</p>","documents":[{"t":"The shop's board","html":"<p><strong>Package A</strong>: 1 GB, valid 7 days, 500 FCFA. <strong>Package B</strong>: 6 GB, valid 30 days, 4 500 FCFA. <strong>Package C</strong>: 15 GB, valid 30 days, 10 000 FCFA. — Night bonus on B and C: +1 GB between midnight and 6 a.m. — Renewal: automatic if you have enough airtime.</p>"}],"question":"How do we ask for information and choose a phone or internet package in English?","tache":"Learn the vocabulary of phone and internet services and the expressions to ask, compare and subscribe, then act out Ngwa's conversation with the shop assistant.","hypotheses":["Pointing at a poster is enough: “That one!”","The cheapest package is always the best.","We ask about the price, the data and the validity, compare the offers with our needs and budget, then subscribe politely."]},"parties":[{"t":"The vocabulary of phone and internet services","html":"<div class='def'><b>Package (bundle)</b>An offer that gives a quantity of calls, SMS or internet data for a fixed price and a fixed period (the validity): for example 6 GB for 30 days at 4 500 FCFA.</div><ul><li><strong>Services</strong>: <em>a package / a bundle, data (MB, GB), airtime (credit), calls, SMS, a SIM card, a network, coverage</em>.</li><li><strong>Conditions</strong>: <em>the price, the validity (7 days, 30 days), a bonus, automatic renewal, terms and conditions</em>.</li><li><strong>Actions</strong>: <em>to subscribe (to), to unsubscribe, to top up, to renew, to activate, to check your balance</em>.</li><li><strong>People and places</strong>: <em>a customer, a shop assistant, a customer service, a phone shop, an agent</em>.</li></ul><p class='formule'>package = data (GB) + validity (days) + price (FCFA)</p><div class='ex'><b>Words in context</b><em>I'd like to top up 5 000 francs of airtime, then subscribe to the 6 GB monthly bundle.</em></div><div class='attention'><b>Attention</b>“Valid for 7 days” means the data disappears after 7 days, even if you have not used it.</div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"Three packages","legende":"Each package combines a quantity of data, a validity and a price.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 210' role='img' aria-label='Three columns: packages A, B and C' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>The shop's offers</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='112.66666666666667' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>A</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>1 GB</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>7 days</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>500 FCFA</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ for a week</text><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='320' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>B</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>6 GB</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>30 days</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>4 500 FCFA</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ for a month</text><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C62828' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C62828'/><text x='527.3333333333334' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>C</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>15 GB</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>30 days</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>10 000 FCFA</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C62828'>→ heavy use</text><text x='634' y='205' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>“That one!” is not enough: Ngwa took package A (1 GB, 7 days) without knowing it would last only a week. Before subscribing, a customer asks questions about the data, the validity and the price.</p>","verdicts":[[0,"rejetee","Pointing without asking leads to the wrong package."]]},"retenir":"package / bundle, data, GB, airtime, validity ; to subscribe, to top up, to renew, to activate."},{"t":"Asking for information and comparing","verrou":true,"illus":{"legende":"Which package for Ngwa?. Needs: about 6 GB for 30 days; budget: 5 000 FCFA.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 210' role='img' aria-label='Three columns comparing the choices for Ngwa' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Needs and budget</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='112.66666666666667' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>A × 6</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>6 GB</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>but 7-day validity</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>renew every week</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ risky</text><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='320' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>B</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>6 GB + night bonus</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>30 days</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>4 500 FCFA</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ fits</text><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C62828' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C62828'/><text x='527.3333333333334' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>C</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>15 GB</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>30 days</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>10 000 FCFA</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C62828'>→ over budget</text><text x='634' y='205' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}},{"t":"Subscribing politely","verrou":true},{"t":"Vers le BEPC","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","c":"3e","rang":105,"m":"anglais","payant":true,"quiz":[],"apc":{"module":"Media and Communication","famille":"Vie sociale et culturelle","agir":"Communicate about media and communication","situation":"In Bamenda, Ngwa needs about 6 GB a month for his online revision and has 5 000 FCFA. In the phone shop, he points at the first poster (1 GB, 7 days), and his cousin says to always take the cheapest package.","tache":"Learn the vocabulary of phone and internet services and the expressions to ask, compare and subscribe, then act out Ngwa's conversation with the shop assistant."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
VRT_L("3e-anglais-listening-complaints",{"titre":"Listening: complaining about service quality","duree":35,"famille":"Media and communication","agir":"Listen to a customer's phone call to a customer service, identify the problem, the request and the solution, and complain politely","accroche":"In Ebolowa, Mrs Mengue's internet has not worked for five days, but the company still took 15 000 FCFA from her account. She calls the customer service and shouts. The agent hangs up. Her daughter Linda listens to a recorded model call. What should her mother have said?","intro":"Linda, a pupil in Ebolowa, listens to a model phone call to a customer service to help her mother complain about her internet. The call will help you learn the vocabulary of complaints and the strategies to listen for the problem, the request and the solution.","objectifs":["use the vocabulary of complaints: a complaint, to complain, a fault, out of order, a refund, compensation, a reference number, customer service","listen to a phone call for the problem, the dates, the request and the solution","recognise polite complaint expressions: I'm calling to complain about…, I'm afraid that…, I would like…","note a reference number, an amount and a deadline correctly"],"enquete":{"titre":"Five days without internet","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='A woman angry on the phone, a router with a red light, a telecom mast and a girl listening with headphones' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='rcC' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#FFEBEE'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F7F3EA'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#rcC)'/><rect y='176' width='640' height='44' fill='#EFEBE9'/><rect x='520' y='30' width='8' height='146' fill='#B0BEC5'/><rect x='500' y='50' width='48' height='6' fill='#C62828'/><rect x='380' y='140' width='70' height='20' rx='4' fill='#263238'/><circle cx='436' cy='150' r='4' fill='#E53935'/><g transform='translate(120 92)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#2E7D32'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#5A3A1E'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/></g><g transform='translate(250 96)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#7B3F99'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#6B4423'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#6B4423'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#6B4423'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#6B4423'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#6B4423'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#6B4423'/></g><path d='M238 92Q250 78 262 92' stroke='#263238' stroke-width='3' fill='none'/><rect x='20' y='20' width='330' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#EF9A9A'/><text x='185' y='40' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>I'm calling to complain about…</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"In Ebolowa, Linda listens to a model call to help her mother complain politely.","contexte":"<p>Mrs Mengue shouts: “Your company are thieves! Repair it now!” The agent ends the call. Linda thinks: “If you shout, they listen.” Her brother says: “Don't complain, it's useless.” Linda's English class has a recorded call of a customer who complains politely; she must find the problem, the dates, the request, the solution and the reference number. The monthly subscription costs 15 000 FCFA for 30 days.</p>","documents":[{"t":"The recorded call (transcript)","html":"<p><strong>Agent</strong>: “Good morning, customer service, Paul speaking. How can I help you?” — <strong>Customer</strong>: “Good morning. I'm calling to complain about my internet connection. It has been out of order since Monday, the 3rd, so five days now. I'm afraid this is not acceptable, because I paid fifteen thousand francs for the month.” — <strong>Agent</strong>: “I'm very sorry about that. Can I have your customer number, please?” — <strong>Customer</strong>: “It's C-4-7-2-9.” — <strong>Agent</strong>: “Thank you. There is a fault on the line in your area. A technician will come tomorrow, before noon. You will also get five days free on your next bill. Your complaint reference is R-1-8-5.” — <strong>Customer</strong>: “Thank you for your help.”</p>"}],"question":"How do we listen to a complaint call and complain politely in English?","tache":"Learn the vocabulary of complaints and the listening strategies, then complete the complaint form from the model call and prepare Mrs Mengue's polite call.","hypotheses":["Shouting and insulting is the best way to get a solution.","Complaining is useless: companies never listen.","We listen for the problem, the dates, the request and the solution, and we complain politely with facts and a clear request."]},"parties":[{"t":"The vocabulary of complaints","html":"<div class='def'><b>Complaint</b>A statement saying that a product or a service is not satisfactory, with a request to correct the problem: a repair, a replacement, a refund or a compensation.</div><ul><li><strong>Problems</strong>: <em>out of order, a fault, a breakdown, slow, poor quality, a wrong bill, overcharged</em>.</li><li><strong>Requests</strong>: <em>to repair, to replace, a refund, compensation, a discount, to send a technician</em>.</li><li><strong>Details</strong>: <em>a customer number, a reference number, a date, an amount, a deadline</em>.</li><li><strong>People</strong>: <em>a customer, an agent, a technician, the customer service, the manager</em>.</li></ul><p class='formule'>problem + facts (dates, amount) + request = a clear complaint</p><div class='ex'><b>A complaint in two sentences</b><em>My internet has been out of order for five days. I would like a technician to come and a refund for the days without service.</em></div><div class='attention'><b>Attention</b>“To complain about something” (se plaindre de), “a complaint” (une réclamation). Do not say “to complain for”.</div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"The parts of a complaint","legende":"A good complaint gives the problem, the facts and the request.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 210' role='img' aria-label='Three columns: problem, facts and request' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>A clear complaint</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C62828' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C62828'/><text x='112.66666666666667' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Problem</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>out of order</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>slow connection</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>wrong bill</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C62828'>→ what</text><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='320' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Facts</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>since Monday 3rd</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>5 days</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>15 000 FCFA</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ proof</text><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='527.3333333333334' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Request</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>send a technician</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>a refund</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>compensation</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ what I want</text><text x='634' y='205' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>Shouting and insulting make the agent defensive: Mrs Mengue's call ended without any solution. A complaint works when it is polite and gives facts the agent can check.</p>","verdicts":[[0,"rejetee","Shouting ends the conversation: be polite and factual."]]},"retenir":"complaint, to complain about ; out of order, fault ; refund, compensation ; reference number, deadline."},{"t":"Listening for the key information","verrou":true},{"t":"Complaining politely","verrou":true},{"t":"Vers le BEPC","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","c":"3e","rang":108,"m":"anglais","payant":true,"quiz":[],"apc":{"module":"Media and Communication","famille":"Vie sociale et culturelle","agir":"Communicate about media and communication","situation":"In Ebolowa, Mrs Mengue's internet has been out of order for five days although she paid 15 000 FCFA for the month. She shouts at the customer service agent, who hangs up; her son thinks complaining is useless.","tache":"Learn the vocabulary of complaints and the listening strategies, then complete the complaint form from the model call and prepare Mrs Mengue's polite call."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
